  </div>

  <div class="apple-tech">
    <h2>At Home on the Mac</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Light and Dark Mode.</b> Warm paper by day and a warm dark page at night, following your Mac’s appearance.</li>
      <li><b>VoiceOver.</b> Every diagram describes itself, naming each chord tone, and Identify announces the chord it finds.</li>
      <li><b>The keyboard.</b> Every control is reachable, and in Identify the arrow keys walk the fretboard or the piano while Return marks a note.</li>
      <li><b>Reduce Motion.</b> The CAGED map changes its highlight without animation when Reduce Motion is on.</li>
      <li><b>Zoom.</b> Zoom In, Zoom Out, and Actual Size in the View menu (⌘=, ⌘−, ⌘0) enlarge the whole sheet to read from guitar distance, and the app remembers the size.</li>
      <li><b>Printing.</b> The Mac’s own print panel, with real page margins and extra room on the hole-punch side. Zoom never changes what prints.</li>
      <li><b>Save as PDF.</b> From the print panel, already named for the sheet you’re looking at.</li>
      <li><b>Mac menus.</b> Full Screen from the Window menu, and the Services, Hide, and Quit items every Mac app has.</li>
      <li><b>Remembers where you were.</b> The window reopens where you left it, at the size you left it, on the instrument, view, and chord you were last on.</li>
      <li><b>Updates.</b> Check for Updates… sits under About Music Prism, and the app checks on its own and tells you when there’s a new version.</li>
      <li><b>Signed and notarized.</b> Signed with an Apple Developer ID and notarized by Apple, so it opens like any other app.</li>
      <li><b>Your mail app.</b> Report a Bug or Request a Feature, in the Help menu, drafts the email in your own mail app for you to send. Every one is read.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
